==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|had}}, {{m|enm|hed}}, {{m|enm|hod}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|hād||person, individual, character, individuality, degree, rank, order, office, holy office, condition, state, nature, character, form, manner, sex, race, family, tribe, choir}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*haiduz||appearance, kind}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kāi-||light, bright, shining}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|hēd||consition, rank}}, {{cog|goh|heit||person, personality, sex, condition, quality, rank}}, {{cog|non|heiðr}} {{gloss|"honour, dignity"}} (whence {{cog|da|hæder||honour}}, {{cog|sv|heder||honour}}), {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐌳𐌿𐍃||way, manner}}. Same as {{l|en|-hood}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|had}}, {{l|en|haid}} {{qualifier|Scotland}}
* {{l|en|hod}}, {{l|en|hode}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|obsolete}} [[person|Person]] (in all senses).
# {{label|en|obsolete|biological}} [[sex|Sex]]; [[gender]].
# {{label|en|Now|_|chiefly|_|dialectal|Scotland}} [[order|Order]]; [[estate]]; [[rank]]; [[degree]]; holy or religious orders.
# {{label|en|Now|_|chiefly|_|dialectal|Scotland}} [[state|State]]; [[condition]]; [[quality]]; [[kind]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|hadien}}, {{m|enm|hodien}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|hādian||to ordain, consecrate}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|hād||rank, order, office, holy office}}. See above.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|hode}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|had}}

# {{label|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[ordain]]; [[consecrate]]; [[admit]] to a religious order.

